  "term": "cued recall",
  "definition": "Cued recall is a memory task in which a person is given a prompt to help retrieve learned information, such as hearing the first word of a pair and recalling the second. In the supplied example, it is used in a child memory assessment with repeated learning trials before later recall without cues.",
